  "note": "Twelve candidates were nominated for the nine seats, including seven outgoing members (Hutchinson, Gracey, Best, Fred Harvey, McKinney, Sinton and Cullen). W. F. Gillespie, Fred Harvey and Robert Reid withdrew by 3 p.m., and the remaining nine were declared elected. William Gribben and Joe Thompson did not seek re-election. Returning officer Joseph Sterling."
